  "question": {
    "text": "A small coin of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is placed on the horizontal surface of a rotating disc. The disc starts from rest and is given a constant angular acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mtext>&nbsp;rad&nbsp;s</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The coefficient of static friction between the coin and the disc is <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mtext>s</mtext> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mn>3</mn> <mo>/</mo> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;and the coefficient of kinetic friction is <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mtext>k</mtext> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mn>0.5</mn> </mrow> </math>. The coin is placed at a distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> from the centre of the disc. The magnitude of the resultant force on the coin exerted by the disc just before it starts slipping on the disc is :<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0014_cc479a49f547.jpg\" style=\"width: 175px; height: 179px;\" />"
  },
